  "body": "### Summary\nOn 2026-11-05 every merge was blocked for hours by the required check \"Analyze (swift)\" (CodeQL, ~15 min on `macos-26`): its jobs were cancelled before any macOS runner picked them up. Meanwhile \"App build + tests (iOS 27 simulator)\", the check that actually caught bugs today, is not required. Operator decision (2026-11-05): apply items 1, 2 and 3 below. Child parallelism stays unchanged.\n\n### Scope\n1. **CodeQL Swift leaves the PR gate.** It still runs on every push to `dev-swift`. On a PR it runs only when the PR carries the `codeql` label (for sensitive changes: session, cookies, posting). It is removed from the required checks in `.github/rulesets/dev-swift.json`. \"Analyze (actions)\" stays required (it runs on Linux).\n2. **\"App build + tests (iOS 27 simulator)\" becomes a required check.** A PR that does not touch the app still passes, because the job is skipped and a skipped job counts as passed (same pattern as today).\n3. **macOS jobs skip draft PRs.** \"HFRKit tests (macOS) + iOS 27 build\" and \"App build + tests\" run on a PR only once it is ready for review (`ready_for_review` triggers them). Linux jobs keep running on every push. GitHub refuses to merge a draft, so the skip never lets one through.\n4. Update the docs: CONTRIBUTING merge criteria, ADR 0005 (amendment), the Operating rules on #368 (children open their PRs as drafts and mark them ready on their last push), and the label `codeql` in `.github/labels.yml`.\n\n### Not in scope\nNumber of parallel children (operator: unchanged).\n\n### Acceptance\n- On a PR to `dev-swift`: a docs-only change runs no macOS job; a draft PR runs no macOS job; marking it ready runs the app and engine jobs it needs; adding `codeql` runs \"Analyze (swift)\".\n- The maintainer re-imports the ruleset (`scripts/configure-repo.sh`). Until then the old required list applies.\n\n/claim cloud/orch",
